{
  "kanji": "苗",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 苗\ntitle: seedling; young plant\njlpt: 1\ntags: [jlpt-n1, grade-8, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 8\nradical: 艸\nradicalNumber: 140\nonyomi: [ビョウ, ミョウ]\nkunyomi: [なえ, なわ-]\nquizOnyomi: [ビョウ, ミョウ]\nquizKunyomi: [なえ, なわ-]\ndistractors: [猫, 留, 畜]\n---\n\n# 苗 — seedling; young plant\n\n**Strokes:** 8 · **Key (radical):** 艸 (as 艹, no. 140) · **JLPT:** N1 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n苗 names a **seedling or young plant**, especially one being raised for planting out. [苗](../words/苗.md) なえ can refer to rice seedlings, but is not limited to rice. 苗木 (なえぎ) specifies a sapling or young tree.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic, not etymology:** Picture the plant-shaped 艹 above a small [田](田.md)-shaped growing plot. Imagine young plants waiting to be moved into a field. This is a memory aid, not a historical derivation.\n\nThe canonical radical 艸 appears in its upper form 艹.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ビョウ | on | [育苗](../words/育苗.md) いくびょう - raising seedlings; 育 supplies イク and 苗 ビョウ |\n| ミョウ | on | [苗字](../words/名字.md) みょうじ - family name; the existing 名字 article also teaches this spelling |\n| なえ | kun | [苗](../words/苗.md) なえ - seedling; young plant |\n| なわ- | kun | [苗代](../words/苗代.md) なわしろ - rice-seedling bed; なわ- is the combining form of 苗 here |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [苗](../words/苗.md) なえ - seedling\n- [育苗](../words/育苗.md) いくびょう - raising seedlings\n- [苗代](../words/苗代.md) なわしろ - rice-seedling bed; also read なえしろ\n- [苗字](../words/名字.md) みょうじ - family name; also written 名字\n\n## Notes\n\n- [芽](../words/芽.md) め is a sprout, shoot or bud; it can occur on a mature tree. 苗 presents a young plant, not every bud on an established plant.\n- Do not translate 苗字 literally as \"seedling character.\" It is the same family-name word as 名字, with a different spelling.\n- The dash in なわ- marks a bound form, not a separately pronounced syllable or a standalone word なわ.\n- [猫](猫.md), cat, adds 犭 to the left of 苗. [留](留.md), retain or stay, and [畜](畜.md), livestock, have different shapes above their lower 田.\n\nMetadata: [KANJIDIC2](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/KANJIDIC_Project), 2026-11-02 snapshot. Word families: [JMdict](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/JMdict-EDICT_Dictionary_Project), entries 1490470, 1490500, 1160750, 1490490, 1604730 and 1197710. Bound-form evidence: [Seisenban Nihon Kokugo Daijiten: 苗代](https://kotobank.jp/word/%E8%8B%97%E4%BB%A3-108702).\n",
